صلاة ربّي مدّ الزّمانِ / على النّبيّ طاهرِ الجنانِ
Ṣalātu rabbī madda z-zamānī / ʿala n-nabiyyi ṭāhiri l-janānī
May my Lord's blessing, for all the length of time, be upon the Prophet, pure of heart —

مَا لاحَ برقٌ وسحَّ رعدٌ / ودامَ ذكرُكَ باللّسانِ
Mā lāḥa barqun wa saḥḥa raʿdun / wa dāma dhikruka bi-l-lisānī
as long as lightning gleams and thunder pours, and as long as your remembrance lives on the tongue.



نسيمُ نجدٍ سرى سُحَيرًا / فجدَّدَ الشوقَ والمَبانِي
Nasīmu najdin sarā suḥayrā / fa-jaddada sh-shawqa wa-l-mabānī
The breeze of Najd travelled in the last dark of night and made longing — and its old dwellings — new again.

وهبَّ ريحُ الصَّبا بِرَوحٍ / مُخبِرًا عن عُرَيبِ بانِ
Wa habba rīḥu ṣ-ṣabā bi-rawḥin / mukhbiran ʿan ʿuraybi bānī
The east wind blew with sweet relief, bearing news of the dear Arab folk who have gone.



يا أهلَ نجدٍ حياةَ روحي / رعاكمُ اللهُ بالأمانِ
Yā ahla najdin ḥayāta rūḥī / raʿākumu llāhu bi-l-amānī
O people of Najd, O life of my soul — may God keep you in safety.

أخذتمُ العقلَ بل فؤادي / جمالُكم سادتي سبانِي
Akhadhtumu l-ʿaqla bal fuʾādī / jamālukum sādatī sabānī
You took my reason, my heart as well; your beauty, my masters, has taken me captive.



وعاذلي رامَ لي سُلُوًّا / فكيف ذا والهوى رمانِي
Wa ʿādhilī rāma lī sulūwan / fa-kayfa dhā wa-l-hawā ramānī
My reproacher wished forgetfulness for me — how could that be, when love has already struck me down?

وحبُّكم في الحشا مقيمٌ / وزدتُ شوقًا وصرتُ فانِي
Wa ḥubbukum fi l-ḥashā muqīmun / wa zidtu shawqan wa ṣirtu fānī
Your love dwells settled in my depths; my longing only grew, until I passed away in it.



وفي رُباكم حبيبُ قلبي / جميلُ ذاتٍ جليلُ شانِي
Wa fī rubākum ḥabību qalbī / jamīlu dhātin jalīlu shānī
In your hills is the beloved of my heart — beautiful in essence, exalted in rank.

من حازَ حُسنَ الصّفاتِ طُرًّا / وسادَ في سائرِ المعانِي
Man ḥāza ḥusna ṣ-ṣifāti ṭurran / wa sāda fī sāʾiri l-maʿānī
He who gathered every excellent quality without exception, and surpassed all others in every respect.



وفاقَ ظبيًا كحيلَ عينٍ / وخصَّهُ اللهُ بالمَثانِي
Wa fāqa ẓabyan kaḥīla ʿaynin / wa khaṣṣahu llāhu bi-l-mathānī
He outshone the kohl-eyed gazelle, and God singled him out with al-Mathānī (the oft-repeated verses).

وعمَّ كلَّ الأنامِ جودًا / ونالَ ما لم ينلْهُ ثانِي
Wa ʿamma kulla l-anāmi jūdan / wa nāla mā lam yanalhu thānī
His generosity encompassed all mankind, and he attained what no second soul has attained.



أثنى عليه الإلهُ مدحًا / فما ثنائي وما بيانِي
Athnā ʿalayhi l-ilāhu madḥan / fa-mā thanāʾī wa mā bayānī
God Himself has praised him — so what is my praise worth, what is my eloquence?

وذكرُهُ في الكتابِ يُتلى / فأعجزَ العَدَّ بالبَنانِ
Wa dhikruhu fi l-kitābi yutlā / fa-aʿjaza l-ʿadda bi-l-banānī
His mention is recited in the Book, past all counting on the fingers.



طوبى لمن قد رآكَ حقًّا / ليتي رأيتُكَ في المنامِ
Ṭūbā li-man qad raʾāka ḥaqqan / laytī raʾaytuka fi l-manāmī
Blessed is the one who has truly seen you — would that I might see you in a dream.

وفي مديحِكَ لستُ أهلًا / لكن صبانِي ذوو الغرامِ
Wa fī madīḥika lastu ahlan / lākin ṣabānī dhawu l-gharāmī
I am no fit man to praise you, yet the passionate lovers have drawn me to it.



وعندما سفرٌ طويلٌ / أرجوكَ يا منتهى المرامِ
Wa ʿindamā safarun ṭawīlun / arjūka yā muntaha l-marāmī
And when the long journey comes, it is you I hope in, O utmost goal of every desire.